{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":27603,"name":"LCL","username":"LusoCryptoLabs","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/talk.nervos.org/lusocryptolabs/{size}/11500_2.png","created_at":"2026-11-19T22:26:36.452Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eCKB Pulse started six weeks ago as \u003ca href=\"https://talk.nervos.org/t/ckb-pulse-who-is-building-on-ckb-live/10862\"\u003eone page that shows who is building on CKB, live\u003c/a\u003e. It has grown into something larger: a place where the work of every CKB builder is seen, credited, and turned into lessons the next builder can use. This post is what it does today.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eVIDEO:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ca href=\"https://x.com/LusoCryptoLabs/status/2123541495776940150\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eLuso Crypto Labs on X: \"Who's building on CKB right now? CKB Pulse shows it, live. And every fix a builder ships becomes a lesson for the next one: 198 so far, each linked to its commit. In your AI agent and on your pull requests. Free and open source. https://t.co/ICccqV4x2Q\" / X\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/original/2X/b/bce1afc7c59e06aba083569fcc9ef2f9ec37d709.jpeg\" data-download-href=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/bce1afc7c59e06aba083569fcc9ef2f9ec37d709\" title=\"CKB Pulse, the live view\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/b/bce1afc7c59e06aba083569fcc9ef2f9ec37d709_2_690x431.jpeg\" alt=\"CKB Pulse, the live view\" data-base62-sha1=\"qWVile8ihxiQ4Mmio5xrsxvmssN\" width=\"690\" height=\"431\" srcset=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/b/bce1afc7c59e06aba083569fcc9ef2f9ec37d709_2_690x431.jpeg, https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/b/bce1afc7c59e06aba083569fcc9ef2f9ec37d709_2_1035x646.jpeg 1.5x, https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/b/bce1afc7c59e06aba083569fcc9ef2f9ec37d709_2_1380x862.jpeg 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"161411\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003eCKB Pulse, the live view\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e1800×1125 249 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003caside class=\"onebox allowlistedgeneric\" data-onebox-src=\"https://pulse.lusocryptolabs.com\"\u003e\n  \u003cheader class=\"source\"\u003e\n      \n\n      \u003ca href=\"https://pulse.lusocryptolabs.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eCKB Pulse\u003c/a\u003e\n  \u003c/header\u003e\n\n  \u003carticle class=\"onebox-body\"\u003e\n    \n\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://pulse.lusocryptolabs.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eCKB Pulse\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n  \u003cp\u003ePulse shows the public work of the CKB ecosystem as it happens, from GitHub: projects, people and updates in one place.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\n  \u003c/article\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv class=\"onebox-metadata\"\u003e\n    \n    \n  \u003c/div\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv style=\"clear: both\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-27603-in-short-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27603-in-short-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eIn short\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLive.\u003c/strong\u003e Every push, pull request, review, issue and release in the CKB projects on GitHub, as it happens. In the 30 days to 19 November: 5,514 updates by 213 people in 209 projects, not counting our own. Bots and AI agents are left out.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eA new look.\u003c/strong\u003e The whole site was redesigned, in dark and light, with a first page that says what it is.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLessons from real fixes.\u003c/strong\u003e 198 lessons so far, drawn from the public commits of 47 CKB projects. Each one is checked against the commit it came from and links to it.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCredit where the work was done.\u003c/strong\u003e Every project has a card with who works on it and what CKB learned from it. Maintainers can confirm the lessons from their own project.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eInside your tools.\u003c/strong\u003e An MCP server for AI agents, a check of your code against the lessons, and a GitHub Action that brings the lessons to your pull requests.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFree and open source\u003c/strong\u003e (MIT), in English, 中文 and Português, on a phone or a computer.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-27603-a-new-look-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27603-a-new-look-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eA new look\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe site was redesigned from top to bottom: straight corners, strong type, one red signal, and the name of who makes it under the title. The reading pages follow your device in dark or light, and you can switch. First-time visitors land on a page that says what Pulse is before the live view opens.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/original/2X/e/ed8d34ccf2ad753aa8974438e6703d4843e007be.jpeg\" data-download-href=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/ed8d34ccf2ad753aa8974438e6703d4843e007be\" title=\"The weekly digest, dark and light\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/e/ed8d34ccf2ad753aa8974438e6703d4843e007be_2_477x500.jpeg\" alt=\"The weekly digest, dark and light\" data-base62-sha1=\"xTtGZNF4OpxXRpgbGzqOdM9OEEK\" width=\"477\" height=\"500\" srcset=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/e/ed8d34ccf2ad753aa8974438e6703d4843e007be_2_477x500.jpeg, https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/e/ed8d34ccf2ad753aa8974438e6703d4843e007be_2_715x750.jpeg 1.5x, https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/e/ed8d34ccf2ad753aa8974438e6703d4843e007be_2_954x1000.jpeg 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"767470\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003eThe weekly digest, dark and light\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e1414×1480 275 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe address changed too: \u003ccode\u003epulse.lusocryptolabs.com\u003c/code\u003e. Old links keep working.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-27603-what-the-ecosystem-learned-kept-for-the-next-builder-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27603-what-the-ecosystem-learned-kept-for-the-next-builder-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhat the ecosystem learned, kept for the next builder\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMost of what builders learn on CKB stays in a commit message, or in nobody’s notes. Someone finds out that an absolute epoch \u003ccode\u003esince\u003c/code\u003e needs its flag, or that \u003ccode\u003ecompleteFeeBy\u003c/code\u003e adds a change output where they expected an output to shrink, fixes it, and moves on. The next builder hits the same wall.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePulse reads the public commits of the projects it follows and keeps what they teach as short lessons: the rule, why it matters, the code before and after when the commit shows it, and the commit itself. A lesson is released only after it is checked against that commit and against the project’s code as it is today. A lesson that stops being true comes down.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/original/2X/5/5c437033c07eaabce366fc315f4782adc0fb1139.jpeg\" data-download-href=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/5c437033c07eaabce366fc315f4782adc0fb1139\" title=\"A project card with its lessons, the lessons page, and a confirmed lesson\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/5/5c437033c07eaabce366fc315f4782adc0fb1139_2_690x486.jpeg\" alt=\"A project card with its lessons, the lessons page, and a confirmed lesson\" data-base62-sha1=\"dacpC9lGyaXJMlz0GV7zUL79i0F\" width=\"690\" height=\"486\" srcset=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/5/5c437033c07eaabce366fc315f4782adc0fb1139_2_690x486.jpeg, https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/5/5c437033c07eaabce366fc315f4782adc0fb1139_2_1035x729.jpeg 1.5x, https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/5/5c437033c07eaabce366fc315f4782adc0fb1139_2_1380x972.jpeg 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"262625\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003eA project card with its lessons, the lessons page, and a confirmed lesson\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e2101×1480 684 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eBrowse and learn:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ca href=\"https://pulse.lusocryptolabs.com/learned\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eCKB Pulse · What CKB learned\u003c/a\u003e, by topic and by level, with a start page, a glossary and a review mode.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCredit:\u003c/strong\u003e every lesson names the project and links the commit. Every project card lists “What CKB learned from this project”.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eConfirmed by maintainers:\u003c/strong\u003e if you own a project, wrote the commit, or are a public member of its organisation, you can confirm or correct its lessons from the lesson page, one by one or all at once. A confirmed lesson shows your name. The first 21 are confirmed, all from our own repositories. Yours are next, if you want them to be.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eOpen data:\u003c/strong\u003e all of it as JSON, under CC BY 4.0: \u003ca href=\"https://pulse.lusocryptolabs.com/learned.json\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003ehttps://pulse.lusocryptolabs.com/learned.json\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-27603-the-lessons-come-to-you-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27603-the-lessons-come-to-you-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eThe lessons come to you\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eReading a list of lessons is one way. Having them arrive while you work is better.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003e\nIn your AI agent\u003c/summary\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePulse is an MCP server. One line in Claude Code (other MCP clients take the same address):\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-auto\"\u003eclaude mcp add --transport http ckb-pulse https://pulse.lusocryptolabs.com/mcp\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYour agent can then ask who works on what, search the lessons, and check your code against them (\u003ccode\u003echeck_code\u003c/code\u003e): it returns the lessons about the functions, RPC methods and constants your code uses, and flags code that repeats a known mistake. It gives hints to read, not proof. Nothing is run and the code is not stored.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo have your agent do this by itself, paste the short rule from \u003ca href=\"https://pulse.lusocryptolabs.com/use#rule\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eCKB Pulse · What you can do with CKB Pulse\u003c/a\u003e into your project’s \u003ccode\u003eAGENTS.md\u003c/code\u003e or \u003ccode\u003eCLAUDE.md\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003e\nOn every pull request\u003c/summary\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA GitHub Action comments on each pull request with the lessons that apply to the lines that changed, repeated mistakes first. Copy one file into \u003ccode\u003e.github/workflows/\u003c/code\u003e:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/LusoCryptoLabs/ckb-pulse-action\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eGitHub - LusoCryptoLabs/ckb-pulse-action: GitHub Action: comments on CKB pull requests with the lessons from real fixes that apply to the changed lines · GitHub\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo key and no account. Only the changed lines are sent, and they are not stored.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/original/2X/4/484a0ae1e6933a065d32370e4bd2686190fc4832.jpeg\" data-download-href=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/484a0ae1e6933a065d32370e4bd2686190fc4832\" title=\"The comment the action leaves on a pull request\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/4/484a0ae1e6933a065d32370e4bd2686190fc4832_2_557x500.jpeg\" alt=\"The comment the action leaves on a pull request\" data-base62-sha1=\"ajv0OO2B5zJW45ZaOwZUP95uIDg\" width=\"557\" height=\"500\" srcset=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/4/484a0ae1e6933a065d32370e4bd2686190fc4832_2_557x500.jpeg, https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/4/484a0ae1e6933a065d32370e4bd2686190fc4832_2_835x750.jpeg 1.5x, https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/4/484a0ae1e6933a065d32370e4bd2686190fc4832_2_1114x1000.jpeg 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"1B2028\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003eThe comment the action leaves on a pull request\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e1400×1255 451 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-27603-who-builds-on-what-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27603-who-builds-on-what-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWho builds on what\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhich CKB libraries do projects really use? Pulse reads the dependency files of every project it follows. The list is made by use: a library appears when several builders use it, and leaves by itself when nobody builds on it any more.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/original/2X/4/401d7e5cd6f27478cae5f1959cf3f4b9f68f98ef.jpeg\" data-download-href=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/401d7e5cd6f27478cae5f1959cf3f4b9f68f98ef\" title=\"Who builds on what\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/4/401d7e5cd6f27478cae5f1959cf3f4b9f68f98ef_2_690x431.jpeg\" alt=\"Who builds on what\" data-base62-sha1=\"99bKmMXNYF6hK5nLrdeSnl1Us8v\" width=\"690\" height=\"431\" srcset=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/4/401d7e5cd6f27478cae5f1959cf3f4b9f68f98ef_2_690x431.jpeg, https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/4/401d7e5cd6f27478cae5f1959cf3f4b9f68f98ef_2_1035x646.jpeg 1.5x, https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/4/401d7e5cd6f27478cae5f1959cf3f4b9f68f98ef_2_1380x862.jpeg 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"191818\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003eWho builds on what\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e1800×1125 177 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eToday: CCC in 124 projects, ckb-std in 89, ckb-testtool in 77, Molecule in 36, and nine more. If you maintain a library, this is your reach, updated twice a day: \u003ca href=\"https://pulse.lusocryptolabs.com/impact\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eCKB Pulse · Who builds on what · CCC\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-27603-also-there-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27603-also-there-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eAlso there\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDigests\u003c/strong\u003e for the day, the week and the month: the busiest projects and people, and what shipped. \u003ca href=\"https://pulse.lusocryptolabs.com/digest?p=week\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eCKB Pulse · Last 7 days\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFollow\u003c/strong\u003e projects and people on your device, and share what they ship.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eA badge\u003c/strong\u003e for your README, and a feed.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAn API\u003c/strong\u003e for everything on the page: \u003ca href=\"https://pulse.lusocryptolabs.com/use\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eCKB Pulse · What you can do with CKB Pulse\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-27603-limits-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27603-limits-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eLimits\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eGitHub only. On-chain activity, private repositories and work outside GitHub do not show.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eProjects are found automatically, by the CKB libraries they use and by how they describe themselves. A check today found about 60 active projects Pulse was missing, and most are followed now. Some are surely still missing: suggest yours on the page.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eA lesson comes from one project’s commit unless it says otherwise. Read the source before you rely on one.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIf you want your project or your account out of Pulse, open an issue and it is done: \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/LusoCryptoLabs/ckb-pulse/issues\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eIssues · LusoCryptoLabs/ckb-pulse · GitHub\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-27603-questions-for-you-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27603-questions-for-you-8\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eQuestions for you\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWhat should Pulse answer that it does not today?\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIf you maintain a project with lessons on Pulse: are they right? Your confirmation, or your correction, makes them worth more to everyone.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWould you put the action on your repository? What would stop you?\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"poll\" data-poll-charttype=\"bar\" data-poll-name=\"poll\" data-poll-public=\"false\" data-poll-results=\"always\" data-poll-status=\"open\" data-poll-type=\"regular\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"poll-container\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"poll-title\"\u003eWhat would you use most?\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli data-poll-option-id=\"bdf8d08a21a6af72496617b5307cd434\"\u003eFollowing projects and people live\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli data-poll-option-id=\"7de223bd59c7e9b896af11acf05cf77c\"\u003eThe daily, weekly and monthly digests\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli data-poll-option-id=\"7721bac67cc12031be47dce2c9efe517\"\u003eThe lessons from real fixes\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli data-poll-option-id=\"fc645a5e311326b5777b280e215d3392\"\u003ePulse inside my AI agent (MCP)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli data-poll-option-id=\"b0b687596dcec4b4b4f8c2f1916af534\"\u003eThe lessons on my pull requests (GitHub Action)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"poll-info\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"poll-info_counts\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"poll-info_counts-count\"\u003e\n\u003cspan class=\"info-number\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003cspan class=\"info-label\"\u003evoters\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSource: \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/LusoCryptoLabs/ckb-pulse\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eGitHub - LusoCryptoLabs/ckb-pulse: Live GitHub activity of the CKB ecosystem, drawn in 3D · GitHub\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCorrections are welcome.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-11-19T22:26:36.452Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":4,"reads":23,"readers_count":22,"score":234.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":11268,"topic_slug":"ckb-pulse-today-a-new-look-lessons-from-real-fixes-and-ckb-inside-your-tools","display_username":"LCL","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_co